condition_name: Chronic Otitis Media
condition_slug: chronic-otitis-media
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "A chronic inflammatory condition of the middle ear mucosa associated with recurrent ear discharge, often over a period of years."
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features of Chronic Otitis Media
    features[5]: recurrent ear discharge (mucoid in simple type; thick and foul-smelling in serious type),increasing deafness,pain is uncommon,central eardrum perforation is of varying size,cholesteatoma and marginal or attic perforation in serious type
investigations[5]: Ear swab for MCS,"Audiogram: conductive deafness","X-ray of the mastoids: shows sclerosis, Hypopneumatization","CT Scan of Petromastoid: Axial, coronal views",MRI of the petromastoid
treatment:
  goals[2]: To give the patient a safe and dry ear,To preserve or restore hearing as much as possible
  non_drug[3]: Careful ear toileting and regular ear dressing with antiseptic pack,Myringoplasty to protect middle ear and improve hearing in dry ears with persistent perforation.,Mastoid operation when there is cholesteatoma unresponsive to treatment.
  drug[4]: Co-Amoxiclav,"Adult: 500/125 mg orally q8hr for 14 days in acute exacerbations.","Child: 6 - 12 years: 250 mg orally 12 hourly","Child: under 6 years: 125 mg 12 hourly"
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[1]: Do not use topical ototoxic antibiotics in the presence of perforation.
  supportive_measures[1]: Protect ears from water with Vaseline/cotton wool while bathing
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[4]: "Intracranial suppuration (extradural abscess, meningitis, or brain abscess)",Lateral sinus thrombosis,Facial nerve paralysis,Labyrinthitis
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null